{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Sanderson&limit=10&title=Volt Rush","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":{"title":"Volt rush","subTitle":"the winners and losers in the race to go green"},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Sanderson, Henry",{"@type":"termsOfAddress","#text":"(Journalist)"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2022"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2022"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"London, England :"}},"publisher":"Oneworld,","dateIssued":"2022."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"viii, 275 pages ; 25 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"In the twentieth century, wealth and power was dictated by access to oil. This century will have different kingmakers, perhaps different wars. We depend on a handful of metals and rare earths to power our phones and computers. Increasingly, we rely on them to power our cars and our homes. Whoever controls these finite commodities will become rich beyond imagining. Sanderson journeys to meet the characters, companies, and nations scrambling for the new resources, linking remote mines in the Congo and Chile's Atacama Desert to giant Chinese battery factories, shadowy commodity traders, secretive billionaires, a new generation of scientists attempting to solve the dilemma of a 'greener' world.\"--Publisher."},"tableOfContents":"Introduction -- The battery age -- Dashed hopes: the troubled history of the EV -- The breakthroughs: the lithium-ion revolution -- China's battery king -- The Chinese lithium rush -- Chile's buried treasure -- The cobalt problem -- The rise of a cobalt giant -- Blood cobalt -- Dirty nickel -- The green copper tycoon -- The final frontier: mining the deep sea -- Reduce, re-use, recycle: a closed loop -- The world's greenest battery -- Cornwall's mining revival.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Henry Sanderson."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Rare earth industry","Environmental aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Rare earth metals","Economic aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Clean energy industries"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Green technology","Economic aspects"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Terres rares","Industrie","Aspect de l'environnement"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Métaux des terres rares","Aspect économique"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Énergies propres","Industrie"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Technologie de protection de l'environnement","Aspect économique"]},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Clean energy industries"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":["Green technology","Economic aspects"]},{"@authority":"fast","topic":["Rare earth industry","Environmental aspects"]}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HD9539.R32 S26 2022"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc","#text":"338.2/7494"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"ebook version :","@displayLabel":"ebook version :"},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99156431001503941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#te